# Sylla Environment Variables
# ============================
# Sylla is part of the Syllabus Sync ecosystem: it shares the SAME Supabase
# project (and therefore the same user accounts) as the main app.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Every variable is OPTIONAL for local dev — with none set, Sylla runs fully
# in anonymous demo mode with mock AI responses and NO quota enforcement.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit .env.local to git - it contains secrets!

# ===================
# SUPABASE (shared with Syllabus Sync) — public/browser-safe
# ===================
# Copy these two values from the Syllabus Sync .env.local (the variable
# names are intentionally identical). Do NOT create a separate Supabase
# project for Sylla.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ===================
# SUPABASE SERVICE ROLE — SERVER-ONLY, required for quota enforcement
# ===================
# Powers the sylla_reserve_*/sylla_finalize_* RPCs that enforce every chat
# and file-upload limit (see docs/quota-and-cost-control.md). Never expose
# this with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Without it, quota enforcement is SKIPPED
# entirely (loudly logged) — do not run a real Gemini key in production
# without this set.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ===================
# SHARED SESSION (production deployments) — public/browser-safe
# ===================
# When Sylla is deployed at sylla.syllabus-sync.app, set the auth cookie's
# parent domain so a Syllabus Sync login is visible to Sylla (and vice
# versa). The same value must be configured in Syllabus Sync's Supabase
# clients. Leave UNSET for local dev.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.syllabus-sync.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=

# ===================
# APP URLS — public/browser-safe
# ===================
# Base URL of the Syllabus Sync deployment (its /login page is Sylla's
# sign-in flow, and /settings hosts account management).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SYLLABUS_SYNC_URL=https://www.syllabus-sync.app

# Sylla's own public URL. Used for docs/redirect configuration; add it to
# the Supabase Auth allowed redirect URLs when shared login ships.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SYLLA_URL=https://sylla.syllabus-sync.app

# ===================
# ANONYMOUS ABUSE-RESISTANCE SALT — SERVER-ONLY, recommended
# ===================
# Any long random string, used to salt the SHA-256 hash of anonymous users'
# IP addresses (raw IPs are never stored). Without it, anonymous rate
# limiting relies on the cookie alone, which is easier to bypass by
# clearing cookies. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SYLLA_IP_HASH_SALT=

# ===================
# AI PROVIDER (Google Gemini) — SERVER-ONLY, optional
# ===================
# Never expose this with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Get a key from
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# If missing, /api/sylla/chat streams a clearly-labelled mock reply and the
# UI shows "Mock AI mode" — the app is fully usable without it.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# Overrides the Gemini model. Never let users select this — it is read
# server-side only. Verify any override against the live ListModels
# endpoint for your project before changing it (see
# docs/quota-and-cost-control.md).
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
